# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  THE FIRST LINE IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS.
#  JobSweep.local.psd1 holds your commute boundary and your employer watchlist.
#  Published, it is a map of your job search. Confirm it is ABSENT from a
#  commit -- `git status` and the full diff -- not merely present-and-ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Wildcards, so a copy ("JobSweep.local - Copy.psd1") is covered too; the
#  shipped example is the one exception.
JobSweep.local*.psd1
!JobSweep.local.example.psd1

# Your own profile assertions. Every line is a statement about where you will
# and will not travel.
Test-JobSweepProfile*.ps1

# Personal copies: Claude Code instructions (CLAUDE.local.md) and filled-in
# prompts such as prompts/build-tracking-board.local.md hold your paths,
# workflow and criteria -- not for publishing.
*.local*.md

# A local tracking board holds your notes and stages. It is written beside
# Sweeps\, which is this folder when no OutputRoot is set.
job-board*.html

# ---- run output ----
logs/
Sweeps/
_seen.json
*.log
*.csv
candidates.json

# ---- editor and OS scratch ----
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.tmp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
